// Changes a tree's list cannot take in where they happen (Inputs/
// tree_moves.ent): the tree is built again for them when the system that
// made them ends, which is also where a cycle is found.
// RUN: %ent build %S/Inputs/tree_moves.ent -o %t.exe 2>/dev/null
// RUN: not --crash %t.exe > %t.out 2>&1
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out

// CHECK:      1: root 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: x 11
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: y 101
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: z 1011
// x, and z with it, under y, which came after x.
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: root 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: x 111
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: y 101
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: z 1111
// The root under a new node.
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: root 6
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: x 116
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: y 106
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: z 1116
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: above 5
// y under z, which is under x, which is under y: no fourth frame.
// CHECK-NOT:  4:
